        "readme": "<h1>HexOS</h1> <p>Everything you love, on a server you own. <a href=\"https://hexos.com\">HexOS</a> is a force multiplier for the TrueNAS you already run, not a replacement: install it here, claim the server at deck.hexos.com, and get the Command Deck on top of the pools, shares, users and apps you have today. Over a hundred curated apps and VMs that install in one tap, HexOS Anywhere to reach every app from anywhere with your network closed, Buddy Backup to a friend's server, the Hardware Advisor watching your exact parts, and notifications a human can read. The full TrueNAS UI stays put.</p> <p>This app is the installer: it marks the server as a HexOS system and serves a single \"Claim this server\" page. After you claim the server at deck.hexos.com with its TrueNAS admin password, HexOS replaces this app with its own HexOS app and keeps the app's data. If the server already runs HexOS, the app removes itself.</p> <!-- x-readme:warnings:start -->  <p><strong>!!! WARNING !!!</strong></p> <p>This application requires additional elevated permissions beyond standard containerization protections. Use at your own risk.</p> <p>The following additional privileges may be enabled from installing this application:</p> <p>\u2022 Docker Socket Access</p> <p>\u2022 Host Networking</p> <!-- x-readme:warnings:end -->",
        "changelog": null,
